From: Andrea Campanella <emuboy85@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ata: pata_ps2: Reset the ATA bus before the probe

The driver never resets the ATA bus of the SPEED interface. The system
software (ATAD) writes SPD_IF_ATA_RESET to SPD_R_IF_CTRL, then 0 and
0x48, and sets PIO mode 0 before it looks for a disk. An original IDE
disk answers without that, a SATA bridge in the bay does not: the port
comes up with "PATA max UDMA/66" and no device.

Do the same reset in the probe, and print the ATA status afterwards.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [PlayStation 2 port]

--- a/drivers/ata/pata_ps2.c
+++ b/drivers/ata/pata_ps2.c
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/init.h>
 #include <linux/blkdev.h>
+#include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/ata.h>
 #include <linux/libata.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
@@ -419,6 +420,21 @@
 
 	iop_set_dma_dpcr2(IOP_DMA_DPCR2_DEV9);
 
+	/*
+	 * Reset the ATA bus of the interface, as the system software (ATAD)
+	 * does before it looks for a disk, and set PIO mode 0 for the
+	 * identification. Without the reset a SATA bridge in the bay stays
+	 * silent, and the port reports no device.
+	 */
+	outw(SPD_IF_ATA_RESET, SPD_REGBASE + SPD_R_IF_CTRL);
+	udelay(100);
+	outw(0, SPD_REGBASE + SPD_R_IF_CTRL);
+	outw(0x48, SPD_REGBASE + SPD_R_IF_CTRL);
+	msleep(3);
+	outw(0x92, SPD_REGBASE + SPD_R_PIO_MODE);
+	dev_info(&pdev->dev, "ATA bus reset, status %02x\n",
+		ioread8(ap->ioaddr.status_addr));
+
 	err = pata_ps2_cmd_bb(pp);
 	if (err < 0)
 		goto err_bb_cmd;
